COMMAND SYNTAX
	appscan <command> [options]
ADDITIONAL COMMAND HELP
	appscan help <command>

DESCRIPTION
	Command-line interface for Static Analyzer. 

GLOBAL COMMANDS
	update               Check for and apply Static Analyzer updates.                                    
	checkUpdate          Check if an update is available.                                                
	version              Display the Static Analyzer version.                                            
	help                 Display available Static Analyzer commands.                                     

REPORT COMMANDS
	get_report           Retrieves a specific report type for a given scan or application ID.            

RESULTS COMMANDS
	get_result           Retrieves the results from the analysis service.                                

CONFIGURATION COMMANDS
	prepare              Generate an IRX file.                                                           
	package              Package an assessment (.ozasmt) file into an IRX file.                          
	get_pubkey           Retrieves the service's active public key and saves it here: <client_utility>/config/rsa.pub 
This key can be used to encrypt data for transmission to the service.
	prepare_sca          Generate an IRX file for Software Composition Analysis (SCA).                   

AUTHENTICATION COMMANDS
	api_login            Authenticate to the service using an API key.                                   

ANALYSIS COMMANDS
	cancel               Cancel a queued or running analysis job.                                        
	list                 List queued, running, and completed analysis jobs (maximum of 2,000 scans returned).
	list_apps            List applications                                                               
	queue_analysis       Submit an IRX file in the current directory for analysis in the cloud.          
	status               Display the status of an analysis job.                                          
	info                 Display the information of an analysis job.                                     
